### Page 1 of 3

```text
2101 O’Neil Ave. · Cheyenne · Wyoming
Phone 307.638.4385
www.plancheyenne.org

MEMO

TO:
Honorable Mayor Patrick Collins and Members of the City Council
FROM:
Ginni Stevens – Senior Transportation Planner, Cheyenne MPO
DATE:
October 17, 2023
SUBJECT:
A Resolution Certifying the Van Buren Corridor Plan
______________________________________________________________________________

The Cheyenne MPO is pleased to have completed the Van Buren Corridor Plan which will amend the
Connect 2045 Master Transportation Plan regarding the future design and reconstruction Van Buren
Avenue between Dell Range and Lincolnway. The Cheyenne MPO retained Y2 Consultants to complete
this study and address roadway deficiencies, traffic safety problems, traffic volume growth,
multimodal needs, drainage constraints, and aligned roadway functionality and character with
existing and planned land uses and desired character.

After extensive public participation, the plan was finalized and presented to the MPO Citizens
Advisory and Technical Committee as well as the City Planning Commission, all of which
recommend adoptions.

Please reach out to me directly if you have any questions regarding this plan.  I can be reached at 638-4384
and gstevens@cheyennempo.org.
```

### Page 2 of 3

```text
RESOLUTION NO. __________

ENTITLED: "A RESOLUTION CERTIFYING THE VAN BUREN CORRIDOR PLAN
AND ADOPTING THE VAN BUREN CORRIDOR PLAN AS AN
AMENDMENT TO THE CONNECT 2045 OF THE CHEYENNE AREA
MASTER TRANSPORTATION PLAN REGARDING THE FUTURE
DESIGN AND RECONSTRUCTION OF VAN BUREN AVENUE
BETWEEN DELL RANGE AND LINCOLNWAY."

WHEREAS, Van Buren Avenue between Dell Range and Lincolnway is classified as a
Major Collector, with jurisdictional responsibility by both the City of Cheyenne and Laramie
County;

WHEREAS, Van Buren Avenue between Dell Range and Lincolnway is a corridor that
varies in width and currently carries between roughly 1,200 and 2,500 vehicles a day, which is
expected to significantly increase by 2045;

WHEREAS, the Cheyenne Metropolitan Planning Organization (MPO) retained Y2
Consultants on October 10, 2022, to develop the Van Buren Avenue Corridor Plan;

WHEREAS, the Van Buren Avenue Corridor Plan identified and addressed roadway
deficiencies, traffic safety problems, traffic volume growth, multimodal needs, drainage
constraints, and aligned roadway functionality and character with existing and planned land uses
and desired character;

WHEREAS, the Van Buren Avenue Corridor Plan and resulting preliminary design
provides the City of Cheyenne, Laramie County, and future developers adjacent to the corridor
with a strategy of investments to meet the transportation and utility needs along the corridor into
the future;

WHEREAS, public involvement for the project consisted of two public meetings, January
25, 2023 and June 1, 2023, to gather feedback on issues and recommendations;

WHEREAS, the plan was developed with the assistance and guidance of a Project Steering
Committee, and presentations to the MPO’s Citizen and Technical Advisory Committees during
the plan’s development;

WHEREAS, the MPO Citizens Advisory and Technical Committees reviewed the Van
Buren Avenue Corridor Plan and recommended adoption by the MPO Policy Committee; and

WHEREAS, the City of Cheyenne Planning Commission held a public hearing on October
16, 2023, accepted public comments, and recommended approval.

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY
OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING, that Governing Body of the Cheyenne Governing Body of the City
8:30 pm, Oct 16 2023
```

### Page 3 of 3

```text
of Cheyenne, Wyoming hereby certifies the Van Buren Avenue Corridor Plan and adopt the “Van
Buren Avenue Corridor Plan” as an amendment to Connect 2045 the Cheyenne Area Master
Transportation Plan.

FURTHERMORE, BE IT RESOLVED, that the Van Buren Avenue Corridor Plan will be
used as guidance for the future design and reconstruction of Van Buren Avenue between Dell
Range and Lincolnway.

PRESENTED, READ AND ADOPTED this _______ day of _____________________,
2023.

